Below is one small change in lib/cli.js that will allow ESLint to support async formatters. The root cause of the problem is that printResults was calling the formatter’s format method synchronously:

• If you write a formatter whose format method returns a Promise (e.g. because you’re using an async highlighter like shiki), ESLint will not wait for it and will either print “[object Promise]” or drop your output entirely.  
• By simply awaiting the returned value, we fully support both sync and async formatters.

